        "name": "DMZ and Joint Security Area",
        "description": "A guided visit to the heavily guarded border between North and South Korea.",
        "details": "DMZ tours go from Seoul to the Dora Observatory, the Third Infiltration Tunnel and Imjingak. The Joint Security Area at Panmunjom is a special tour needing early booking and passports. Dress codes apply and photography is restricted in places. Tours are cancelled during tensions.",
        "interests": [
          "culture",
          "authentic_local",
          "iconic_landmarks"
        ],
        "mobility": "L",
        "image": null
      },
      "south-korea/gyeongju": {
        "name": "Gyeongju Bulguksa, Seokguram and Daereungwon",
        "description": "The old Silla capital, a museum without walls with temples, royal tombs and a hilltop grotto.",
        "details": "Bulguksa is a UNESCO temple with stone pagodas, and Seokguram Grotto holds a Buddha statue on Mount Toham. Daereungwon is a park of grass-covered Silla royal tombs, and Donggung Palace and Wolji Pond are lovely at night. Rent a bicycle to see the city.",
        "interests": [
          "culture",
          "iconic_landmarks",
          "photography"
